Subject: Port protobuf 3.21's C++ runtime to Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

InternalMetadata and TaggedAllocationPolicyPtr kept tagged pointers in
intptr_t/uintptr_t words, and TaggedStringPtr untagged through a uintptr_t
return value. Integer-typed storage drops the capability, so protoc trapped
("cannot read pointer with null object") on the first message with unknown
fields. Keep them in pointer-typed words and tag with pointer arithmetic.
Inline assembly (ror with a memory operand, flag outputs, bts on memory) is
rejected by Fil-C at run time; use the portable fallbacks.

PROTOBUF_TAILCALL and the version scripts are handled in ports.nix.
Checked by checks.protobuf_21 (tests/protobuf.nix) and the upstream suite.

